cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and record the commit and experiment configuration."
type: software
title: "Multiscale FEM Scattering: GMsFEM and Neural Operators for 2D Helmholtz Wave Scattering"
authors:
  - family-names: Monastyrev
    given-names: Egoriy
repository-code: "https://github.com/Egoriy286/multiscale-fem-scattering"
url: "https://github.com/Egoriy286/multiscale-fem-scattering"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research software for two-dimensional heterogeneous Helmholtz wave scattering.
  The project combines complex-valued P1 finite element reference solutions,
  generalized multiscale finite element methods with elliptic and Helmholtz
  snapshot spaces, POD/SVD coefficient-space spectral neural operators,
  Chebyshev spectral neural operators, and Fourier Neural Operators.
  Docker-based Python workflows support mesh and dataset generation, training,
  inference, consistent FEM L2 evaluation, and mesh-refinement studies.
  Reported neural results describe held-out wave parameters in one fixed medium.
keywords:
  - Helmholtz equation
  - wave scattering
  - heterogeneous media
  - finite element method
  - generalized multiscale finite element method
  - reduced-order modeling
  - proper orthogonal decomposition
  - spectral neural operators
  - Fourier Neural Operator
  - Chebyshev polynomials
  - FEniCSx
  - DOLFINx
